  "worked_solution": "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(xy)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(xy)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{yyx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yyx}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({f}_{yy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(xy)) \\\\  & =-2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(xy)-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(xy)\\cdot y \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
